I’ll inspect the specimen metadata and pattern first, then identify chemically plausible reference structures and build a complete GSAS-II multiphase refinement. I’ll keep phase additions tied to coherent residual peak families and preserve the best physical checkpoint as the final project.

The chemistry points first to BaWO₄ plus possible residual BaO₂/WO₃ or a barium-rich intermediate, but I’m treating that only as a candidate inventory. I’m now extracting the measured peak families and querying the frozen COD index for exact Ba–W–O, Ba–O, and W–O references before refinement.

The first trial exposed two useful issues: the input’s CRLF line endings initially broke the temporary three-column conversion, and COD 1010618 contains an unphysical 0.46 Å O–O contact despite its attractive peak match. I’ve corrected the import and excluded that reference from any final model; the physically valid monoclinic WO₃ references are now being compared on the full grid.

The full-grid comparison favors physical triclinic WO₃ (COD 2106293) with BaO₂: Rwp is 7.18% versus 7.89% for the physical monoclinic alternative, while orthorhombic and other WO₃ models are substantially worse. Both accepted candidates are geometrically sound; I’m now checking whether the remaining residuals form a third-phase family or are intensity/profile mismatches within the two-phase model.

A bounded-coordinate trial was rolled back immediately: stale GSAS-II atom indexing caused the bounds to target the wrong internal variables, collapsing W sites. The saved physical checkpoint was unaffected. I’ve corrected the indexing and am rerunning the heavy-atom step from that checkpoint; only a geometrically screened improvement will be retained.

The two-phase inventory is now complete: every coherent reflection family is assigned, while BaWO₄ and barium-rich candidates lack their diagnostic peaks. Final nuisance/profile refinement gives a physical full-pattern model near Rwp 7.1%; I’m expanding it to the exact input grid, exporting CIFs and the profile, and running consistency/geometry checks on the submitted artifacts.

The exported CIFs and profile passed geometry and numerical checks. One final consistency assertion failed on a bookkeeping detail, so I’m isolating that mismatch before handoff; the scientific values and files remain intact.

Completed and validated.

Result: 65.97 wt% triclinic-like WO₃ (P-1) and 34.03 wt% BaO₂ (I4/mmm), normalized over crystalline phases. Rwp = 7.098%, Rp = 5.333%, GOF = 1.952.

